\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  O Love Divine, how sweet thou art!
\par \pard\li180\sl200\slmult0 When shall I find my willing heart
\par All taken up by thee?
\par I thirst, I faint, I die to prove
\par The greatness of redeeming love,
\par The love of Christ to me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Stronger His love than death or hell;
\par \pard\li180\sl200\slmult0 Its riches are unsearchable;
\par The first-born sons of light
\par Desire in vain its depths to see;
\par They cannot reach the mystery,
\par The length, and breadth, and height.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. God only knows the Love of God;
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0 O that it now were shed abroad
\par In this poor stony heart!
\par For love I sigh, for love I pine;
\par This only portion, Lord, be mine,
\par Be mine this better part.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  Forever would I take my seat
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0 with Mary at the Master's feet;
\par be this my happy choice;
\par My only care, delight, and bliss,
\par My joy, my heaven on  earth, be this,
\par \pard    To hear the Bridegroom's voice.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

